# Customers: No Near-Duplicates

Near-duplicate people (e.g. “Edwin van den Berg” vs “Edwin Van Der Berg”) and similar company labels must not become separate records with split waybills.

## When creating or editing customers

1. Use `KIT_Customers::normalize_person_name_key()` / `normalize_company_compare_key()` and `customer_name_surname_exists()` / `company_name_exists()` — do not weaken these to exact case-only matches.
2. Reject saves that collide with an existing or **similar** name; point the user at the existing `cust_id` (or Merge).
3. Prefer selecting an existing customer on waybill create over inserting a new near-match row.

## When cleaning duplicates

1. **Never** delete a duplicate that still has waybills you want to keep.
2. Use `KIT_Customers::merge_customers($keep_cust_id, $drop_cust_id)` (admin Merge action): reassigns `kit_waybills.customer_id`, retargets portal `kit_customer_id` meta, then deletes only the duplicate customer row.
3. Plain Delete still cascades and **destroys** that customer’s waybills — warn and prefer Merge first.

## Setup Seed / ownership verification

After seed merge collapses near-duplicates, verification must accept remaps when
normalized labels match (`kit_seed_verification_labels_equivalent` /
identity keys). Do not reintroduce exact sheet-id-only checks that fail on
“van den” vs “Van Der”.

## Example

```text
Bad:  create "Edwin Van Der Berg" while "Edwin van den Berg" exists
Good: block create; Merge duplicate → keep one cust_id → all waybills on the keeper
```
